From bd13385fb8f088a0451624d2de61cec1f302f3c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:36:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] feat(ui): one Settings window for the per-user settings

The ribbon's Settings button and a new File > Settings... row open an
in-app Settings window with four sections: Appearance (theme, colour
vision), Graphics (line width, anti-aliasing), Graphics device
(read-only adapter, backend and sample counts) and Updates (check for
updates). Each choice applies at once and goes to prefs.json or
view.json; each section with a setting has "Reset to defaults".

The Settings dropdown is gone. The viewport Display menu loses the line
width and the anti-aliasing; its group "Graphics" is now "View options".

Fixes #4493

